<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › Accessibility</div>
    <span class="eyebrow hero__eyebrow">Accessibility</span>
    <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
    <p>We want everyone to be able to use the <%= SITE.name %> website, whatever their needs.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:800px;">
      <p class="muted">Last updated: <%= updated %>.</p>

      <h2>Our aim</h2>
      <p>We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA, so that everyone can find and compare our homes, book a visit and apply for jobs.</p>

      <h2>What we’ve done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Text and buttons with strong colour contrast, and links that are underlined</li>
        <li>Every page works with a keyboard alone, with a “skip to main content” link and visible focus outlines</li>
        <li>Headings, labels and descriptions that make sense to screen readers</li>
        <li>Text alternatives for meaningful images</li>
        <li>Pages that adapt to phones and tablets, and text you can enlarge up to 200% without losing content</li>
        <li>A “Show” button on password boxes, so you can check what you’ve typed</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Parts that may be harder to use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The map on Find a home</strong> can be difficult with a keyboard or screen reader. Every home is also listed as text on the same page, with the same details.</li>
        <li><strong>The CQC rating box</strong> on a home’s page comes from the Care Quality Commission, and we can’t change how it works. Each home’s rating is also written on the page as text.</li>
        <li><strong>Photo galleries</strong> describe the home in general terms rather than each picture in detail.</li>
        <li><strong>Downloadable documents</strong> such as PDFs may not be fully accessible. Ask us and we’ll provide the information another way.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Information in other formats</h2>
      <p>If you need something from this website in another format — large print, easy read, or read to you over the phone — contact us at <a href="mailto:<%= SITE.email %>"><%= SITE.email %></a> or on <%= SITE.phone %>. We’ll reply within five working days.</p>

      <h2>Tell us about a problem</h2>
      <p>If you find something on this website you can’t use, please let us know using the details above and we’ll put it right. If you’re not happy with our response, you can contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS) at <a href="https://www.equalityadvisoryservice.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">equalityadvisoryservice.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>How we check</h2>
      <p>We check the website ourselves, with a keyboard, a screen reader and automated testing tools, whenever we make significant changes. This statement was last reviewed on <%= updated %>.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:2rem;"><a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary">Contact our team</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
